// "Hold the Line" — Company of Heroes: US Army vs Wehrmacht. The map is cut into sectors; capturing a point takes
// its sector, and a point pays (fuel, munitions, manpower) only while its sector is linked to the headquarters through
// own sectors (supply lines). Victory points drain the enemy's 500 tickets. Manpower trickles in from the HQ and drops
// with a bigger army (upkeep: 85% / 70% / 55% of the income at 30 / 60 / 85 population). Infantry are squads: one hp
// pool split over the men, damage scales with the men alive, reinforced near own buildings. Riflemen and
// Volksgrenadiers throw grenades for munitions. Prices follow CoH (manpower / munitions / fuel / population).
// Not yet here (engine plan): cover, suppression and pinning, retreat, veterancy, facing armor, weapon crews,
// garrisoning houses, doctrines.
